The upstream block defines backend pools. Algorithms: round-robin (default), least_conn, ip_hash (sticky sessions), and hash $request_uri consistent. Keepalive directive maintains warm TCP connections.

#### Production NGINX Directives #032
In edge routing configuration 032, upstream connectivity and security isolation are prioritized.

```nginx
# NGINX configuration block for nginx_upstream_load_balancing #032
upstream backend_cluster_032 {
    least_conn;
    server 10.0.32.10:8080 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    server 10.0.32.11:8080 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    keepalive 32;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name service-032.enterprise.internal;
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/service-032.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/service-032.key;

    location /api/v1/ {
        proxy_pass http://backend_cluster_032;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_read_timeout 32s;
    }
}
```

